## High findings

### UBNT-PERF-001 — Hardware offload disabled

Category: Performance · Confidence: Certain

Affected devices: device-1

IPv4 forwarding offload is disabled on a model with hardware offload. Forwarding may consume more CPU and reduce routing throughput. Check feature compatibility before enabling offload in a maintenance window. Verify offload status and CPU use under representative traffic.

| Device | Metric | Observed | Threshold |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| device-1 | system.offload.ipv4_forwarding | {"address":"address-1","host":"host-1","mac":"address-2","serial":"serial-1","unsafe":"a&#124;&lt;script&gt;\nnext"} | — |

### UBNT-SEC-002 — Public management address

Category: Security · Confidence: Certain

Affected devices: device-1

The enrolled management address is public. Internet exposure increases the chance of unauthorized access if upstream filtering allows it. Put management on a private network or restrict access to trusted source addresses. Verify the upstream access policy and management reachability from outside the network.

| Device | Metric | Observed | Threshold |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| device-1 | management.address | "address-1" | — |

### UBNT-SEC-011 — WAN firewall missing

Category: Security · Confidence: Heuristic

Affected devices: device-1

An EdgeRouter WAN interface has neither an inbound nor a local firewall attached. Forwarded traffic and traffic to the router may lack the intended protection. Confirm the WAN role and attach suitable rules for both traffic paths. Test management access and permitted traffic before closing the maintenance window.

| Device | Metric | Observed | Threshold |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| device-1 | interfaces.eth0.firewall | {"in":null,"local":null,"role":"Wan"} | — |

